  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What is the core idea of anarchism?', 'The rejection of the state and all forms of coercive authority.', 1),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What is collectivist anarchism?', 'Anarchism based on common ownership and cooperation, e.g. anarcho-communism and anarcho-syndicalism.', 2),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What is individualist anarchism?', 'Anarchism prioritising individual sovereignty and rejecting the state, e.g. anarcho-capitalism and egoism.', 3),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What is anarcho-communism?', 'A stateless society with common ownership and distribution according to need.', 4),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What is anarcho-syndicalism?', 'Anarchism using trade unions and general strikes to overthrow capitalism and the state.', 5),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What is anarcho-capitalism?', 'The belief that the free market can replace the state entirely, including provision of security and justice.', 6),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What is egoism?', 'Stirner''s belief that individuals should act solely in their own interest, rejecting all external authority.', 7),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What is Stirner''s contribution to anarchism?', 'He argued the individual ego is supreme, and rejected the state, morality and religion.', 8),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What is Goldman''s contribution to anarchism?', 'She linked anarchism with feminism and opposed the state, religion and marriage as oppressive.', 9),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What is the anarchist view of human nature?', 'Humans are naturally sociable and cooperative (collectivists) or rational and self-interested (individualists).', 10),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What is the anarchist view of the economy?', 'Collectivists want common ownership; individualists want free markets without the state.', 11),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What is the anarchist view of the state?', 'The state is coercive, corrupting and unnecessary.', 12),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What is the anarchist view of society?', 'Society can organise itself naturally without the state.', 13),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What is direct action?', 'Political action outside formal institutions, such as protests, strikes and sabotage.', 14),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What is mutualism?', 'Proudhon''s idea of a society based on voluntary exchange and cooperative banks.', 15),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What is the anarchist critique of religion?', 'Religion is a form of authority that suppresses individual freedom.', 16),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What is the anarchist critique of capitalism?', 'Collectivists argue capitalism exploits workers and relies on the state to protect property.', 17),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What is the anarchist view of liberty?', 'True freedom is only possible without the state.', 18),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What is propaganda by the deed?', 'The use of violent acts to inspire revolution, used by some anarchists in the late 19th century.', 19),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What is the anarchist view of democracy?', 'Representative democracy is a form of domination; anarchists favour direct democracy or none.', 20),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What are the criticisms of anarchism?', 'It is utopian, unrealistic about human nature, and could lead to chaos.', 21),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.7', 'Anarchism', 'What is the anarchist view of economic freedom?', 'Collectivists see economic freedom as freedom from exploitation; individualists as freedom of exchange.', 22),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What is ecologism?', 'An ideology that places the natural environment at the centre of political thinking.', 1),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What is shallow ecology?', 'An anthropocentric approach that protects the environment for human benefit, e.g. sustainable development.', 2),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What is deep ecology?', 'An ecocentric approach that nature has intrinsic value independent of humans.', 3),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What is sustainability?', 'Meeting the needs of the present without compromising future generations.', 4),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What is environmental ethics?', 'The idea that moral consideration should extend to future generations, animals and nature.', 5),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What is ecological consciousness?', 'A deep awareness of humanity''s connection to nature.', 6),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What is Lovelock''s Gaia hypothesis?', 'The Earth is a self-regulating living system.', 7),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What is Carson''s contribution to ecologism?', 'Silent Spring (1962) exposed the damage caused by pesticides, starting the modern environmental movement.', 8),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What is Schumacher''s idea of ''small is beautiful''?', 'Economies should be small-scale, local and sustainable, using appropriate technology.', 9),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What is social ecology?', 'Bookchin''s idea that environmental problems are caused by social hierarchies and capitalism.', 10),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What is eco-socialism?', 'The view that capitalism causes environmental destruction, so common ownership is needed.', 11),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What is eco-anarchism?', 'The belief that small, decentralised communities living in harmony with nature are ideal.', 12),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What is eco-feminism?', 'The view that patriarchy and environmental destruction are linked.', 13),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What is the ecologist view of the economy?', 'Opposition to endless growth; support for a steady-state or zero-growth economy.', 14),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What is the ecologist view of the state?', 'Shallow greens accept the state; deep greens favour decentralised communities.', 15),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What is anthropocentrism?', 'A human-centred view that nature exists for human use.', 16),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What is ecocentrism?', 'A nature-centred view that all life has intrinsic value.', 17),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What is the ecologist view of human nature?', 'Humans are part of nature, not separate from or above it.', 18),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What is the precautionary principle?', 'Taking action to prevent harm even if there is not full scientific certainty.', 19),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What are the criticisms of ecologism?', 'It may be anti-growth and anti-development, and deep ecology is seen as impractical.', 20),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What is green consumerism?', 'Buying environmentally friendly products, criticised by deep ecologists for not tackling underlying problems.', 21),
  ('Politics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '3.8', 'Ecologism', 'What is a steady-state economy?', 'An economy with stable, sustainable levels of population and resource use, rejecting endless growth.', 22)
),
fresh AS (
  SELECT v.* FROM v
  WHERE NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM flashcards f
    WHERE f.subject = v.subject AND f.exam_board = v.exam_board AND f.level = v.level
      AND f.topic_id = v.topic_id AND f.front = v.front)
),
cur AS (
  SELECT subject, exam_board, level, topic_id, count(*) AS n, max(card_order) AS mx
  FROM flashcards
  WHERE subject = 'Politics' AND exam_board = 'AQA' AND level = 'alevel'
  GROUP BY 1, 2, 3, 4
),
ranked AS (
  SELECT fr.*, coalesce(c.n, 0) AS n, coalesce(c.mx, 0) AS mx,
         row_number() OVER (PARTITION BY fr.topic_id ORDER BY fr.ord) AS rn
  FROM fresh fr
  LEFT JOIN cur c USING (subject, exam_board, level, topic_id)
)
INSERT INTO flashcards (subject, exam_board, topic_id, topic_name, front, back, card_order, level)
SELECT subject, exam_board, topic_id, topic_name, front, back, mx + rn, level
FROM ranked
WHERE n + rn <= 30;
